  "briefing": [
    {
      "text": "LOCAL VS GLOBAL SCOPE TEST",
      "size": "large",
      "align": "center"
    },
    {
      "text": "Question: which of LOCAL and GLOBAL values written in one context are visible in another (objective, briefing button, thread, CARLS event handler) and after reload_mission? Each SET writes a marker into one local (LS_x) and one global (GS_x); each READ logs the four locals L[OBJ BTN THR EVT] and the four globals G[...] as seen from the reading context ('-' = not visible)."
    },
    {
      "text": "Suggested order: 1) read the first line (objective SET at start). 2) SET FROM BUTTON, then READ FROM BUTTON. 3) SET FROM THREAD (logs SET at 1 s and READ at 2 s from the thread). 4) ARM CARLS KEYS, sit in the helicopter with the CARLS on, press key 1 (SET from event) and key 2 (READ from event). 5) READ FROM BUTTON again, and READ FROM NEW THREAD. 6) RELOAD MISSION: the objective logs OBJ-RELOAD. 7) READ FROM BUTTON after the reload. Send the 8 lines after every step."
    },
